WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
REau installation and Wi-Fi problems, and how to fix them

2
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:09.267
1. Play Protect blocked the installation. Tap the button at the bottom, Got it

3
00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:15.533
In the Play Store, pause app scanning, install the APK again and turn Play Protect back on

4
00:00:15.533 --> 00:00:21.933
2. Android Auto server off: REau warns that Android Auto didn’t start

5
00:00:21.933 --> 00:00:25.867
Tap Open Android Auto settings

6
00:00:25.867 --> 00:00:30.933
In the three-dot menu, tap Start head unit server

7
00:00:30.933 --> 00:00:39.000
Restarted the phone? The server turns off and the warning returns: start it again by hand. REau connects by itself when it answers

8
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:48.533
3. The menu doesn’t show Start server? Android Auto’s developer mode is off. Scroll to the bottom and tap Version ten times

9
00:00:48.533 --> 00:00:54.800
Confirm with OK. The phone’s developer mode doesn’t count: it has to be Android Auto’s

10
00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:03.600
4. After Turn off, Android Auto takes up to a minute to close the previous session. REau warns you and retries by itself

11
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:10.600
To skip the wait, in the three-dot menu tap Stop head unit server and then Start

12
00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:18.800
5. Android Auto not answering or with no picture: in Settings, Apps, Android Auto, tap Force stop

13
00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:24.000
Then turn REau off and on. In Battery, choose Unrestricted

14
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:29.000
6. If REau shows this warning, a VPN is holding it back

15
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:35.333
Turn the VPN off or leave REau out of it, with split tunneling, and reconnect the VPN

16
00:01:35.333 --> 00:01:43.067
7. Dash Wi-Fi not found: turn the bike’s key on and check the phone’s Wi-Fi and location

17
00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:48.267
In Bike data, tap Show to check the full network name

18
00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:54.400
If you changed bikes or there is more than one dash nearby, tap Forget and search again

19
00:01:54.400 --> 00:02:00.267
The first time, Android asks Connect to device: tap Connect

20
00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:08.067
8. If you see Another app has the dash, stop the other app’s streaming to the dash. REau retries by itself

21
00:02:08.067 --> 00:02:14.600
The dash may have hung: switch the bike off with the key, wait about thirty seconds and switch it on again

22
00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:24.667
9. If the dash shows PICTURE STUCK or the app says No new picture, Android Auto stopped sending the picture. It usually comes back by itself

23
00:02:24.667 --> 00:02:31.533
10. If you turned on the network server, REau doesn’t look for the dash: turn that switch off to use the bike

24
00:02:31.533 --> 00:02:35.667
More answers are in REau’s frequently asked questions

